Unused `Regex`/`Text`? fine. `using System.Windows.Forms` in AutoStart for Application.ExecutablePath. Good.

Now OnlineChecker. Need handle 302 WebException; response may be null. Use `request.AllowAutoRedirect=false`. Check portal body. For `generate_204`, a 200 with zero body online; but if campus returns a portal page with 200 and body markers, offline. For baidu, body may be compressed; AutomaticDecompression. Read first 64KB.

NetworkInterface.GetIsNetworkAvailable can be true with virtual adapters (VMware) only; but requests determine.

Design result:
```
public class OnlineCheckResult {
 public bool Online; public bool NetworkReady; public string PortalUrl; public string Detail;
}
```
- `Detail` no credentials.

`Check`:
```
string configured = NormalizeBaseUrl(configuredPortal);
string discovered = null;
bool gotAnyResponse = false;
string lastError = null;
string[] urls = { "http://connect.rom.miui.com/generate_204", "http://www.baidu.com/" };
foreach...
  try...
  catch WebException ex:
    response = ex.Response as HttpWebResponse;
    if (response != null) { gotAnyResponse=true; handle ... }
    else { lastError=ex.Status...; }
```
Need avoid double `using` for response. Factor `HandleResponse(url, response, configured, out...)` but C# out complexity. Inline.

`IsPortalBody` static public for reuse.
`IsOnlineBody` for baidu: contains "baidu.com" or "百度".
- If status 200 from `connect.rom.miui.com` and body doesn't contain portal markers, maybe it's a proxy error page; treat online only if length 0 or body contains "miui" or status 204. For `generate_204`, 200 with empty is online; 200 with non-empty portal markers offline; otherwise online? Could be captive portal login page. Better: if URL contains `generate_204`, require status 204 or empty body; if non-empty, inspect markers; if no markers, treat online (some proxies return "OK").
- For baidu, require body contains "baidu" or "百度".
- If one endpoint says online, return online immediately.
- If one says offline, remember portal; continue to other endpoint? If portal redirect, online is clearly false; no need. But a blocked endpoint 403 could look offline falsely. We can return online only on positive signal; offline only on portal/redirect. If both fail with no positive, `Online=false, NetworkReady=gotAnyResponse`.
- If `generate_204` returns 302 to `https://...` not portal, `FindPortalUrl` may return null; use configured portal.
- `Location` may be `http://10.110.125.20/?...`; `GetOrigin`.
- If response is 200 portal page, `FindPortalUrl` may parse meta refresh to same host; use `GetOrigin` of that or configured.
- Avoid following redirects to HTTPS (cert issues).

Let's write.

